---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro';
import TrainingJourney from '../../components/TrainingJourney';
import '../../styles/hands-free.css';
import DialMark from '../../components/DialMark';
import { TIMER_PRESETS } from '../../lib/timer-preset.mjs';
---
<Article h1={"Dead hang timer & training log."} subtitle={"Set the intervals. Do the holds. Record what happened. Your log stays in this browser, with export and delete controls."} crumbs={[{"name":"Timer & log"}]} wide title="Dead Hang Timer & Training Log | Free, No Account" description="Time your dead hang sets and rest periods. Record your real holds on your device, compare like-for-like sessions and export your training log.">
<div class="article-body workspace-page"><TrainingJourney client:load /><noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to use the timer and log, or use the <a href="/training-programs/#print-plan">printable planner</a> with your own stopwatch.</p></noscript><h2>Make your log useful</h2><p>Compare the same grip and assistance. Record actual holds after the session; a completed timer does not mean a hold was completed. Export a copy before changing devices or clearing browser storage.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="text-link" href="/training-programs/">Choose a starting plan</a><a class="text-link" href="/dead-hang-calculator/">Compare a hold with your target</a></div><section id="hands-free" class="hands-free" aria-labelledby="hands-free-title"><h2 id="hands-free-title" class="hf-title"><DialMark size={24} /> Use it hands-free</h2><p class="hf-lead">Set the timer once, then open it with one tap, a saved link or a voice command.</p><h3>Preset links</h3><p class="hf-lead">Each link opens the timer with the session already set up. Nothing starts until you tap Start. Save your own setup with Copy link to this setup in the timer options.</p><ul class="hf-presets">{TIMER_PRESETS.map((preset) => (<li><a class="hf-preset" href={preset.path}><span class="hf-preset-name">{preset.name}</span><span class="hf-preset-note">{preset.summary}</span></a></li>))}</ul><p class="small-copy">The Level 1 dose is common training practice, not a tested prescription.</p><h3>Add it to your home screen</h3><ul class="hf-steps"><li>iPhone or iPad in Safari: tap Share, then Add to Home Screen, then Add.</li><li>Android in Chrome: open the menu, then tap Install app or Add to Home screen.</li></ul><h3>Ask Siri to open it</h3><ol class="hf-steps"><li>Open the Shortcuts app and tap the plus button to start a new shortcut.</li><li>Tap Add Action, search for Open URLs and choose it.</li><li>Tap the URL field and paste a preset link from above. Press and hold a link and choose Copy Link to copy it.</li><li>Tap the shortcut name at the top, choose Rename, and call it Dead hang timer.</li><li>Tap Done, then say "Hey Siri, dead hang timer". The timer opens set up. Tap Start when you are on the bar.</li></ol><p><a href="/bar-card/">Print a bar-side card</a> with a QR code for each preset. Vibrate on changes appears in the timer options only in browsers that support it.</p></section></div>
</Article>
